  "note": "Triennial election of the whole council, 18 seats: 39 nominated, reduced to 31 by three withdrawals and five invalid papers, so all three wards were contested. Returning officer T. G. Peel. The stiffest contest: 494 electors, 447 voted; the Nationalists claimed 279 votes and the Unionists 215."
